DMMS Alerts - Aviation Stall Warning App

<a href="https://youtube.com/shorts/amdtjvCtZW0?si=LJ8sUriT-sw1b_fp">Watch on YouTube</a>

[Intro - App Launching]
Welcome to DMMS Alerts, your personal aviation stall warning system.

[Main Screen - Top Section]
At the top, you see your GPS speed in knots... your altitude in feet... and your heading in degrees.

The status shows MONITORING when actively tracking... PAUSED when you've stopped... or LANDING MODE when approaching an airport.

Below that, the DMMS threshold picker lets you set your stall speed anywhere from 1 to 270 knots.

[Alert Section]
When your speed drops below the DMMS threshold, the screen turns RED and the warning triangle appears with a voice alert saying your custom message like, "Speed check! Stall warning!"

[Compass Rose]
On the right, the compass rose shows the direction to the nearest airport. The label below tells you which airport, and shows which heading to turn to - either left or right, whichever is shortest.

[Bottom Section]
At the bottom, you see the closest airport information including distance in miles, the bearing, and the field elevation.

The Start/Pause button controls monitoring.

[Options Page]
Tapping Options takes you to the settings page.

Here you can configure:
- Alert frequency - how often the warning repeats
- Weather fetch interval - how often METAR updates
- Airport callouts toggle
- Show warning icon toggle  
- Auto-start monitoring on app launch
- Ground or car mode for testing on the road
- Custom alert message
- Custom app title
- Traffic pattern callouts - within a set distance from the airport, you'll hear callouts at 700 feet, 500 feet, and 100 feet above ground level

[Summary]
That's DMMS Alerts - keeping you aware of your speed and proximity to airports with customizable warnings and voice alerts.